 6. Capacity/debug (GET/DELETE need S2; budget/eviction parts run now): lower the tip budget,
-   alternate enough lines to force eviction. Require pinned roots to survive, tip bytes within
-   budget, exact-prefix matching (two unrelated same-length lines must not cross-match), and the
-   disk dir within cap after background writes settle. After S2: GET `/v1/cache` inventory and
-   DELETE dropping non-pinned tips only. Record peak host RAM and retained lines; the fork
-   budget must hold at least depth+1 intended lines.
+    alternate enough lines to force eviction. Require pinned roots to survive, tip bytes within
+    budget, exact-prefix matching (two unrelated same-length lines must not cross-match), and the
+    disk dir within cap after background writes settle. After S2: GET `/v1/cache` inventory and
+    DELETE dropping non-pinned tips only. Record peak host RAM and retained lines; the fork
+    budget must hold at least depth+1 intended lines.
+
+## S2 cache API (GET/DELETE /v1/cache)
+
+Same auth as `/v1/models` (Bearer or x-api-key; 401 without a valid key when configured). GET and DELETE are supported; unknown GET/DELETE paths return 404.
+Engines without a cache pipe are 501 `unsupported` (MockEngine, which speaks the pipe, reports the
+honest empty inventory). A cache call waits for the Service FIFO behind any running/queued request,
+bounded (30 s): past that it answers 503 busy without sending anything or disturbing the active
+generation. A dead engine is 503; an ERR/malformed reply is 503 only after its remainder is consumed
+to a response boundary — otherwise the engine is stopped for a clean restart (a late ERR must never
+reach a future generation) and later cache calls fail until a generation restarts it.
+
+`GET /v1/cache` answers the SavedState inventory:
+
+```json
+{"memory": {"tip_budget_bytes": 8589934592, "tip_bytes": 6789,
+            "items": [{"kind": "root", "pinned": true, "ids_len": 2048, "bytes": 12345,
+                       "last_use": 7},
+                      {"kind": "tip", "pinned": false, "ids_len": 4096, "bytes": 6789,
+                       "last_use": 9}]},
+ "disk": {"enabled": true,
+          "items": [{"kind": "root", "pinned": true, "ids_len": 2048, "bytes": 123456}]}}
+```
+
+`DELETE /v1/cache` drops all non-pinned tips only (pinned memory roots and every disk root survive)
+and answers `{"dropped": <tips dropped>, "memory": {...}, "disk": {...}}` in the GET shape.
+
+Semantics the owner relies on:
+
+- `memory.items` lists roots first, then tips. `tip_budget_bytes` is the `--tip-cache-gib` budget,
+  `tip_bytes` the live tip total (within budget after eviction).
+- `last_use` is the RAM LRU clock in store ticks (a per-process monotonic counter advanced by every
+  insert and by every mounted restore via `note_use`), not a wall timestamp. Higher means used more
+  recently; values are comparable only within one engine process lifetime.
+- DELETE removes tips only. The live `ConvCheckpoint` chain (this session's in-progress history) is
+  untouched and keeps serving the next request; pinned memory roots stay pinned.
+- The `disk` section lists indexed roots only (`enabled` says whether root-disk is on at all) as
+  `kind`/`pinned`/`ids_len`/`bytes` metadata — payloads are never loaded for inventory, and disk rows
+  carry no `last_use` (the disk cap trim is LRU by file mtime, not by the RAM clock). The disk index
+  is eventually consistent: a just-captured root appears after the background writer lands it, so a
+  GET immediately after a first-prefix request may not list it yet.
+- The live `ConvCheckpoint` chain is per-request history and is NOT reported: GET covers SavedState
+  roots/tips plus the disk index only.
+- Nothing identifying content leaves the engine: no token ids, no payload bytes, no filesystem paths,
+  no header/identity fields — only lengths, byte counts, kinds, pin flags and the LRU clock.
+- A CACHE command arriving after DONE is answered only after the engine's post-DONE capture
+  completes, so the inventory (or the drop) always reflects the finished request's tip — including
+  the generated tokens the section-7 fork rule requires.
